A||||22||RobertVol||Flames suit on... gotta say this||||1||
Z||000000||RobertVol||10-16-2000||03:57 PM||||I went and looked at a 86 GT today and I am sick and tired of uneducated people selling these things and asking outragous amounts of money. <P>The guys was aking FIRM 3900.00. <P>Now the car has 99,000 miles on it. Bad exhaust manifold leak. (which of course he did not know) He had it completely repainted by God only knows because they painted the mirrors and the overspray was horrible. and the intake vent!and the black strips on the side markers! and missed alot of spots. The interior was OK no tears in the seats. and he did put in a new clutch. and new brakes, But the rear GT lense was cracked and the spoiler had the bad sagging in the middle. Also they painted the bottom that is gray , black and missed there and had bad overspray onto the red. So I looked at it and offered 2900.00 which I thought was generous. He just went off saying this was a classic and that he was asking to little. I am thinking OK I have 3 of these things and drove them for years so but thanks for educating me. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>Did I mention the quarter windows had overspray and were cracked? <P>All this to say I love Fieros and think they are great but every stinking one of them is not a Classic and the few ones that "May" be such as the 88Gt t top and the indy and maybe yeloow formulas. Are the exception.<P>Oh yeah did I mention bad bearings and needs some major suspension work. that thing wondered on the road like a man's eyes at the Playboy mansion! Please! <P>And to make it worse he then says that he will take a hundred off  and I said ok and do the Headlights come up ok? Oh yeah they are great! Uh huh. I opened them and he says see! and then I close them and they start the dropping and then stop and drop and then stop thing! uhhh! <P>OK well sorry for venting its just burns me when people try this crap. Not every Fiero is a classic. Maybe a great car but not a CLASSIC!  If any of them will be. Even our  T topper's  <P>One last thing is what really gets me is somone will pay for this thing the money he asks and then get it home drive it and then run into all the problems I saw and we will have another Bad reputation out there because of an un=educated car saleman! <P>Thanks for letting vent. I feel much better <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT 55k  <BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||10-16-2000||04:14 PM||||Actually I believe silver Formulas are the rare-est of the Formulas.  I though Yellow too at first and many people I talk too say the same.<P>Sounds like you came across a bad deal, just blow it off, many Fiero's in the sea.  Like any sales person selling a sports car they are going to tell you it's "collectable" and "rare"<P>I always say Fieros are Fieros, not Beanie Babies.<P>&lt;grabs the fire extinguisher from my 84, DOH&gt;<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-16-2000||04:40 PM||||.. really and how does that make you feel?... HEH  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> i know what you mean.. a few people asked me while my car was all apart.. "why would you do that to such a rare car"(frame machine guy) or .. " parts for these classic cars are hard to find you'll be at the dealer a lot" (lame neighbor kid) uum funny.. His 98 V6 mustang just got new rear main, VC gaskets and a host of other work and she only got 27k.. hummm.. i'm at 106 (on the odo) and NO problems here... <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
