Z||000008||Jaei Sun||10-16-2000||07:14 PM||||I think I have an even better example of a moron used car dealer.<P>A little while ago I saw a yellow 88 coupe at one of those little corner car dealerships.  Well a friend and I decided to go check it out.  Here's the rundown:<P>88 yellow coupe<BR>Tech 4 w/ 103,000 on it<BR>5 speed<BR>no sunroof, rear win defroster<BR>no pwr mirrors,windows, locks, trunk release<BR>no cruse control, delay wipers<P>For $5000<P>The car had a Spoiler from a Grand AM on it it and it looked like crap, it was too small on the decklid and the yellow didn't match the car.<P>When I drove it I noticed that<BR>- The whole car was squeaking like a mother<BR>- The Speedometer didn't work at all.<BR>- The shifter got stuck in 3rd I had to wiggle it for like I minute to get it out of that gear.<BR>- And in the last 10 minutes of the test drive the "Check Engine" light came on.<P>The guy proceeded to tell me about how this was a rare car.  He also said that he had someone come out  appraise the car and said that's what the car was worth.<P>My friend offered the guy $1000 and the guy started over with "how rare the car was" & "The wing looks like a GT one". Oh and he also said that the car would be great in winter.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/umebottle3/fie_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Sillhouette.com||10-16-2000||08:02 PM||||I will comment on that picture.  It looks good.  Hopefully that we get some pictures in the car with a dyno or 1/4 mile time otherwise it's a lie.  Also hope that you do a better job on it than racetech.  I don't know what garbage they use but they have blown both of the turbo that they built (no wonder)  and one of them was supposed to be a state of the art one.  Good luck and as I said show pictures otherwise it's nothing more than fantasy.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000010||BBBAD GT||10-16-2000||08:26 PM||||Jeez, don't you think that's a little harsh, saying its a 'lie' or 'fantasy' unless he has dyno or 1/4 mi times? <P>Does it look like Travis is bragging or something to say that?  I just don't get that feeling.  Maybe I'm overreacting.....<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||10-16-2000||09:37 PM||||explain how a photo of an engine component, without any claims or explanation, is a lie...<P>I know there's some bad blood between RSM and Race-Tech.. I don't know the reasons, but I do think it's just slightly unprofessional to openly bash someone's business...<P>anyway, back on-topic.. I've also seen some outrageous dealer prices on Fieros.. $4,000 for a below average condition 86 SE, for example.. torn seats.. blown speakers.. scuffed up interior.. etc. and another one I looked at, from a small autobody shop... it had been in an accident! the fender was cracked.. the door panel was pushed in.. one of the engine grilles was missing (85 SE 2M6) the console was warped so much it looked like a semicircle on top.. the steering rack was messed up.. plus many other things.. Dave (forum member) and I went to look at it back in the summer.. he suggested I act like I didn't know much about Fieros, so the guy wouldn't jack up the price for an enthusiast...<BR>anyway, when I asked the seller about it, he wanted $3,500.... so we left.. immediatly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
