Z||000013||fiero56||10-16-2000||10:21 PM||||Just keep looking around, sooner or later you will find what you want, for what you want to pay.<P>I happen to own one of the rarest Fiero body panels ever. It just happens to be the door skin from an original silver '88 Formula, and it is in good shape. Anyone want to buy it, $900 and it's yours. I'll even pay shipping. Just think, you put this on your Fiero, and this body panel will snazz it up nicely, might even have people stop and ask where they can find one like it. I don't know the exact mileage, but its just like slapping in a new low mileage "smooth shifting"...I better shut up before I get myself into trouble <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||007DOUG||10-17-2000||12:01 AM||||RobertVol:<P>Gotta love the prices folks ask for fieros. <P>They aren't YET collector cars.<P>He'll be calling you back. Trust me, Thats how I got all mine. <P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
